[SIZE=5][B]Prerequisites[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Unlocked Bootloader on [B]Realme X2 Pro (RMX1931 / RMX1931L1 / samurai)[/B].
[*][B]Realme UI 2.0 (Android 11, C.36 or newer) firmware[/B] already installed (verified automatically via TrustZone check).
[*][B]TWRP Recovery 3.7.x[/B] for RMX1931.
[*][B]DO NOT flash separate GApps[/B] — Google Play Services & Pixel apps are already included!
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]How to Install — First-Time Clean Flash[/B][/SIZE]
[I](Note: The initial Clean Flash is split into [ICODE]VendorBoot.zip[/ICODE] [~858 MiB] + [ICODE]System.zip[/ICODE] [~1.88 GiB] to stay under GitHub Releases' 2 GiB single-file limit. Once installed, all future updates arrive as lightweight ~6–8 MiB Wireless OTAs!)[/I]
[LIST=1]
[*]Back up all important files from Internal Storage to a PC or USB drive.
[*]Download [B]RMX1931-Android17-PixelOS-VendorBoot.zip[/B] and [B]RMX1931-Android17-PixelOS-System.zip[/B] from the GitHub Releases link below.
[*]Boot into [B]TWRP Recovery[/B].
[*]Go to [B]Wipe -> Advanced Wipe[/B], select [B]Dalvik / ART Cache, Cache, System, Vendor, Data[/B] (do NOT select Persist), and Swipe to Wipe.
[*]Go to [B]Install[/B]:
   - Select [B]RMX1931-Android17-PixelOS-VendorBoot.zip[/B] first.
   - Tap [B]Add more Zips[/B] and select [B]RMX1931-Android17-PixelOS-System.zip[/B] second.
   - Swipe to confirm Flash.
[*]Go to [B]Wipe -> Format Data[/B], type [B]yes[/B], and confirm (required on first clean flash for Android 17 File-Based Encryption).
[*]Tap [B]Reboot -> System[/B]. First boot takes ~2–3 minutes.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]How to Update — Built-in Wireless OTA (No Data Wipe)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Open [B]Settings -> System -> System update[/B] on your phone.
[*]Tap [B]Check for update[/B] -> [B]Download update[/B] (continues in the background or with the screen off).
[*]Once SHA-256 verification finishes, tap [B]Reboot & install[/B] — TWRP automatically installs the update via OpenRecoveryScript and boots back into Android 17 with all your apps and data intact!
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

